NTM Doors
=========

This project is a standalone Minecraft 1.12.2 port of the door system from
HBM's Nuclear Tech Mod (NTM).

Original project and source:
  https://github.com/HbmMods/Hbm-s-Nuclear-Tech-GIT

The following material is derived from HBM's Nuclear Tech Mod and is used
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (LGPL-3.0):

  * Door OBJ models under assets/ntmdoors/models/doors/
  * Door model textures under assets/ntmdoors/textures/models/doors/
  * Door sounds under assets/ntmdoors/sounds/doors/
  * Door geometry, animation dimensions and behaviour used by
    src/main/java/com/ntmdoors/door/DoorDecls.java

Exception: the Black Mesa door test assets
(assets/ntmdoors/models/doors/black_mesa_door.obj,
assets/ntmdoors/textures/models/doors/black_mesa_door.png and
assets/ntmdoors/sounds/doors/door_latch.ogg) are not HBM material.
The door texture is a scaled/cropped derivative of Black Mesa's
materials/metal/bms_metaldoor_2.vtf (Crowbar Collective) and is included for
private testing only; it is not LGPL-licensed and must be replaced or licensed
before public redistribution. The latch sound was supplied by the project owner.

The concrete building set is derived from HBM's Nuclear Tech Mod Community
Edition (NTM CE):
  https://github.com/Warfactory-Official/Hbm-s-Nuclear-Tech-CE

  * Concrete textures under assets/ntmdoors/textures/blocks/
    (concrete*, brick_concrete*, concrete_pillar_*, concrete_rebar.png)
  * Block names, metadata order, material values, recipe layout and the Über Concrete
    decay behaviour used by src/main/java/com/ntmdoors/concrete/

The HL Blocks set is derived from NeoRussia's HL Blocks project:
  https://github.com/NeoRussia/HL-Blocks

  * HL textures and models under assets/ntmdoors/textures/blocks/hlblocks_* and
    assets/ntmdoors/models/{block,item}/hlblocks_*
  * Block definitions, crate stacking and shift-scroll cycling used by
    src/main/java/com/ntmdoors/hlblocks/

HL Blocks is used under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (LGPL-3.0).

The transition seal model was converted from HBM's Collada source
(seal.dae) into a grouped OBJ so the 1.12.2 renderer can display it without
a runtime DAE loader. Its per-group rigid keyframes in
assets/ntmdoors/models/doors/transition_seal.anim were generated from the
same Collada action.

Speaker alarm sounds:

  * assets/ntmdoors/sounds/speaker/facility.ogg is derived from
    "Sirens and Alarm Noise" by aquinn (OpenGameArt, CC0 1.0).
  * assets/ntmdoors/sounds/speaker/air_raid.ogg, industrial.ogg and eas.ogg
    are derived from audio supplied by the project owner. The supplied
    filenames credit jeremayjimenez and 8footdino_on_scratch.

The Java implementation in this repository is a fresh 1.12.2 implementation
and is also released under the LGPL-3.0. See LICENSE.LESSER for the full
license text.

